WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.440
Today's the day that I'll settle the score!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.240
Just surrender already!

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.160
Lyria!

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:21.870
Rackam! Head inside there!

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.630
There's no other way! Go!

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.430
Go after them! Don't let them get away!

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:43.520
H-Hold on a second!

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:45.850
That's the Mist-Shrouded Isle!

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.520
That's the infamous...

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.230
I thought it was just a rumor amongst skyfarers!

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.360
It is no mere rumor!

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:59.070
Not one ship sent to that island
has ever returned.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:02.660
Even our own military has ceased
all exploration attempts, I do say.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.690
Man, that was too close for comfort!

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.980
How did the ship fare, Eugen?

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:56.730
Took some hits here and there,
but she'll fly after a few quick fixes.

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:57.990
Then again...

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:58.990
No good.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.950
Every last instrument got blasted.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.070
This is gonna slow us down...

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.950
Hey, someone give us a hand!

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:08.000
I'll help.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:12.790
Then I'll head to a nearby village
to gather information and food supplies.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.000
I'll go with you.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.210
Something about this island seems strange.

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.970
It makes me uneasy.

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:24.010
Do you think it's a primal beast?

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:29.480
The thing is, it seems like it could be,
but it's different than normal.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.560
I can't tell.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.940
Really? Your special senses are
in a haze or something?

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.530
No wonder! Plenty of fog 'round these parts!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.740
Jeez, this is no joke.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:45.910
The Grandcypher's a wreck, and we've
crash-landed on a creepy, infamous island...

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.200
Creepy's right.

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.370
Sure looks haunted, don't it?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.800
I-It's all right, Lyria.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.810
S-Sorry!

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.140
Maybe you should have just stayed on the ship.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.600
Why'd Eugen have to go and open
his big mouth?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.730
<i>Well, that's cause the mist
around here's got a shady history, see.</i>

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.360
<i>They say if your ship gets swallowed up in it,
you'll never make it out.</i>

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.610
<i>You'll be doomed to wander forever
through the mists, until eventually...</i>

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.740
<i>You're ridin' aboard a ghost ship...</i>

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.490
<i>As a specter yourself!</i>

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.660
P-Please don't remind me!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.380
Eugen, try not to scare Lyria, will you?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:41.510
Even I wouldn't be surprised
if something were to happen in this mist.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.720
My bad! Couldn't help myself.

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:48.100
All right, what's next?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:51.060
Don't be shy. Tell me what to do, Rackam.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:51.770
Huh?

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:54.600
Yeah...

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.270
Let's see...

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.650
Lyria, we're here.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.080
Um, excuse me?

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.640
So sorry he scared you.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:36.350
Everyone's always been terrified of his face, you see.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.600
And it's even worse now!

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.020
What are you talking about?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.570
If anybody here looks like a monster, it's you.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.280
Never thought I'd ever see
a zombie in the flesh...

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:50.030
Wh-What are you talking about, Vyrn?

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:54.160
I-I'm s-sure they just look pale
because they have colds...

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.330
Isn't that right?

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:59.880
Zombies don't catch colds, dear.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.170
Ever since we died,
we've been the picture of health.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.260
Guess you wouldn't know
unless you died yourself,

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.630
but being a zombie ain't all bad.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.760
Well, it seems true enough.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:16.180
R-Right, we'll get used to this in no time!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.940
They all seem like nice people...
Even if they are zombies.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.110
Um, if you don't mind my asking...

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:25.280
Since when have you been in this condition?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.320
You weren't born as zombies, were you?

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.950
Let's see...
What's it been, a hundred years now?

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.000
There was an epidemic
sweeping through the village,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.750
so bad we thought we'd all get wiped out.

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:44.630
That's when the island became shrouded in mist,
and the ghost ship appeared.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:54.010
Ghost ship, you say?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:07:00.270
And no one's been able to die
on this island since.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.860
We've always been a tiny village.

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:06.780
After a hundred years,
you get sick of the sight of each other!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:11.070
It's been so long since we've had
any visitors from outside the island.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.570
Never mind back-to-back!

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:15.200
Back-to-back?

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.410
Someone besides us was here?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.000
Yeah, just a little while ago.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.500
Shall I introduce you? Please, this way!

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:31.840
It's you...

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:33.300
You were with the Black Knight.

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.470
Oh, do you all know each other?

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.680
She was brought here by a pair of mercenaries,
an Erune and a Draph.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:41.850
An Erune...

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.060
And a Draph? Mercenaries?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:45.360
Where are those two now?

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.190
We're back!

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:49.190
Hey, sorry to keep you waiting...

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:50.570
Huh?

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:51.990
You two!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.950
What are you doing here?

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.460
Um, sorry, I just...

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.250
I'm hungry...

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.920
I want food. Now.

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:15.720
This color look funny to anybody else?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.720
Let's dig in!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.310
Hey, you all right?!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.140
Deeeeelicious!

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:26.650
This stew is exquisite!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.030
Don't tell me, are these the phantom shrooms
grown only on Tramont?

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:34.860
I'm impressed you know about 'em.
They're our specialty!

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.500
It's really good!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:50.880
She's right.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:52.670
Wow, this flavor is unbelievable!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.300
Yeah, tastes great!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.840
I've never tasted anything like it!

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:57.340
I shall try it, too.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:04.350
The mushrooms are nice and chewy, aren't they?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:11.530
So, um... I think maybe, um...

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:15.570
I've never had... anything like this... before...

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.950
Phew, I'm stuffed!

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:24.870
Well?

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.330
What are you guys doing in a place like this?

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.460
Right back at you.
What's your reason for being here?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.420
Reason, schmeason!

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:38.300
We had to make an emergency landing
on this island 'cause the empire was chasing us!

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:40.800
Is that so? What a coincidence.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.100
We're here on a little vacation. Aren't we, Sturm?

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:45.810
Vacation?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.310
I've never heard of anyone relaxing
on a mist-covered island!

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.820
Shouldn't you go to a normal spot? Like Auguste!

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.440
Now there's a point!
If you're gonna lie, at least make it sound better!

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.240
Don't look at me.
If you wanna know why, ask him.

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:00.870
Oh please! Sure you want to know?

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.740
Then I'll clue you in as a favor.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:06.410
As rumors have it,
somewhere on this island,

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:09.380
there lies an ultra rare treasure
just waiting to be found!

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:13.460
Come on, what kind of face is that?

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:17.760
You think I would really make up a story
just to get out of a tight spot?

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.720
How cruel! Not you too, Sturm!

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.810
So? Were you able to find that treasure?

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:26.520
Oh, not even close.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.020
Even though we've been walking
all over the island for days.

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:31.650
So here's my proposal.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:35.570
I know it's sudden, but why don't we call
a temporary truce, and help each other out?

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.030
Work together?

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.410
You want us to help with your treasure hunt?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:43.910
Oh, heavens, no. I can handle that myself.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.040
What I need your help with is, well...

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.410
The primal beast.

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.460
There's something preventing us
from leaving this island, you see.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.920
Try as we might, we always end up back here.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.680
Come to think of it,
Rackam mentioned something, too.

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.890
That the instruments were out of whack.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:08.230
Hey, does that mean that
we can't get off this island, either?

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:12.480
An island without death,
where escape is impossible...

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.150
The only thing in the skies that can make that
sort of stuff possible is...

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.150
A primal beast.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:19.610
Bingo!

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.860
After hearing all the stories,
I put two and two together.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:26.990
The ghost ship that appeared a hundred years ago,
it's probably a primal.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:30.330
Not only that, but you guys don't want to turn into
zombies and be stuck here forever, right?

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:35.040
It's not as safe as it's cracked up to be.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.920
They say that the ghost ship eats zombies.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:39.760
It's true.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:44.390
From time to time, it shows up in the village
out of the blue, and starts gorging itself.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.930
See? Sounds like a perfectly good reason for
a little cooperation to me.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.480
I'm too young and handsome
to be a ghost ship's lunch.

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.770
Even so, it's not like we
can join forces just like that!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.230
That's our line!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.240
Even if you say you want to work together,
how're we supposed to trust you?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.740
I-I don't see any problem.

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:07.200
Since we're in the middle of such a crisis.

00:12:07.620 --> 00:12:09.370
Isn't that right, Gran?

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.040
Lyria...

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.170
All right, let's call a temporary truce.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:19.420
Since it doesn't seem like you're planning
to use the primal beast for anything bad.

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:21.630
That's what I like to hear!

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.630
Hey, are you sure?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:26.050
Well, if Gran says so.

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.930
Who said talks are over?
I'm opposed to this idea.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:33.310
What? You'd rather live out your days as a zombie?

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.060
Huh? Don't be absurd!
There's no such thing as zombies.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.740
Hey, what are you talking about?

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.110
This village is teeming with zombies.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.120
Wrong. They've just caught colds,
so they look a little pale.

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.490
Back me up, Drang.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:53.330
Please, how could they not be zom—

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:56.500
Ouch! Ouch, ouch, ouch!

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:00.380
Pretty unusual for you to stay back on the ship.

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:03.470
I was sure that you'd go off with Lyria.

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.630
Well, she has Gran.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.890
Gran's reached the point where I can
leave her with him without worrying.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:15.770
Besides, it's best for Lyria
if I'm not constantly hovering around.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:16.940
You think?

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:23.030
And also, remember how poorly I piloted that
air skimmer? What an embarrassing crash.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.780
Yep, that was a disaster.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:32.450
If I'm going to earn my keep as a skyfarer,
I should at least learn to pilot and maintain airships.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.410
Even if it's just a little bit.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.000
Katalina, you're up!

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:41.500
Sorry, but can you go to the storeroom
and pick another one of these?

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:42.710
Leave it to me.

00:13:45.260 --> 00:13:49.300
She really seems fired up since Albion.

00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:50.930
Just look at her!

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.850
What's with the long face? You feelin' okay?

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.650
This airship...

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:03.530
My dream of gettin' the Grandcypher
off the ground came true.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:07.490
But now what?
Where do I go from here?

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:10.570
Why am I still on this journey?

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.290
Of course, I want to be there for Gran and Lyria.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:19.120
That's my gut instinct, and I doubt my feelings'll
change anytime soon.

00:14:19.120 --> 00:14:24.380
I know that much at least, but...
There's more to it than that.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.470
How should I put it?

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.590
Keep stressin'!

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:34.350
Worrying about the future and
pursuin' your dreams are perks of being young.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:35.680
It's now or never.

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:37.770
Huh? The heck are you talking about?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:39.730
A doctor?

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:44.070
Apparently, he was also studying the primal beast
that appears on this island.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.990
Don't you think it's worth looking into?

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:49.990
You have a point.
It might lead to some kind of clue.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.880
Come to think of it,
we haven't introduced ourselves yet.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.550
I'm Io.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:10.220
This is Lyria. That's Gran and Vyrn.

00:15:10.220 --> 00:15:11.720
What's your name?

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.640
Name?

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.560
That's right.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:20.850
If we don't know, we won't be able to call to you,
and that wouldn't be good, would it?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:26.150
My name is Orchis.

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:28.900
Oh, that's a nice name!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.110
Isn't it, Lyria?

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:34.660
Orchis... Orchis...

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.870
So your name is Orchis.

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:41.170
Rackam, how are the instruments looking?

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.920
It's hopeless.

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:46.420
The machines should be good to go,
yet here we are.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:50.130
I've been piloting for a long time,
but I've never seen anything like this.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.350
That's odd.
Don't tell me this island really is cursed.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.100
I'm gonna go check out the locale.

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:00.600
I'll go pick up Gran and the others
while I'm at it.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:07.730
Whoa, it's like a haunted house!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.450
Um...

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.580
Why don't we talk to that girl over there?

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:20.450
Girl?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:23.670
Wh-Where?

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:25.460
There's nobody there.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:31.470
Oh, please, you're both trying to scare me,
aren't you? I'm not falling for it.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:32.420
Excuse me!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:35.140
Um, do you have a minute?

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.430
Hey, who are you talking to?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.180
What? What do you mean?

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:40.930
She's there.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:46.150
A blue-haired Erune...

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.110
Exactly, the blue-haired girl.

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.360
Oh, please wait up!

00:17:04.080 --> 00:17:07.170
- She really was there!
- Well, she wasn't just seconds ago!

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.340
Drang?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:16.220
You can see me? Really?

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.810
Right... so you can see me.

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.980
Um... Who are you?

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:29.270
I'm...

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.320
I don't know.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.400
You don't know?

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:38.410
Yeah. Not my name, nor what I am.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.780
Nothing at all.

00:17:43.750 --> 00:17:46.170
All right then! We can work with this!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.880
Not having a name is the pits,

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:52.510
so how about we call you "Ferry"
until you remember?

00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.380
I think it's adorable!

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:58.390
Hey! You can't just name people you don't know!

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.300
It's okay...

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:01.600
That will do.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.720
For some reason, it's strangely familiar.

00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:09.150
So that was a hundred years ago, Ferry?

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:13.820
Yeah. When I woke up inside the mist
with most of my memories gone.

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:19.780
All I know is that I've forgotten
something important, or at least I think I have.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:21.580
And that's just so frustrating.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:29.670
I'd wandered all over the island, trying to find out
who I am, and what it is that I've forgotten.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.760
I went to the village, too.
But no one was able to see me.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:41.100
At some point, I wandered upon this place.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.850
I hoped to find a clue here, somewhere.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.440
Maybe something that would lead me
to the memories I'd lost.

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:50.900
You read all of these?

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:53.400
I did have all the time in the world.

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:58.780
Are these medical books?
And literature on the primal beasts?

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:00.410
Fifty-fifty, I'd say.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:05.240
It seems like the owner here was treating illnesses
and using what he'd learned

00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:08.000
to further his research on immortality.

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:11.500
Immortality? Not the primal beast?

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:13.290
Those are both the right answers.

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:17.970
Celeste...

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:20.630
A primal beast said to bring on immortality.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:27.220
They say Celeste used to migrate
across the skies in this area.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.730
There are rumors about her
among skyfarers from way back.

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.730
This island was part of her migration route.

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:37.860
This is the diary of the owner of this house.

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:44.450
Apparently, he came to this island
to summon Celeste and seize her power.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:47.200
The first step was to perform a ritual.

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:52.210
But in order to make that happen,
he needed to offer a living sacrifice.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:57.210
The doctor chose a father-child pair
from among the villagers,

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.630
and made them cooperate by convincing them that
it was all for the sake of curing the epidemic.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.600
"Tomorrow, I shall obtain eternal life at last."

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:09.980
"I will have that pitiful father and his
young daughter sacrifice themselves."

00:20:10.980 --> 00:20:15.150
The diary ends right there,
and I don't know what happened after that.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:20.900
But Celeste really did appear,
the people were turned into living corpses,

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:24.700
and the island was shrouded in mist,
preventing anyone from leaving.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.740
No question about that.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.460
I think I was dragged into the doctor's scheme,
and became like this.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:39.800
Though I searched the entire island,
I couldn't find the doctor, nor the father or child.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.970
So if anyone knows the whole story...

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:46.390
It's got to be Celeste, and Celeste alone.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:58.020
But it doesn't seem like Celeste
can see me either.

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:03.030
For the last one hundred years,
the only people to notice me...

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.870
The only ones who even know of my existence...

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.290
You all are the first.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:14.870
So...

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:22.260
Let's unravel the mystery of Celeste,
and liberate this island.

00:21:23.590 --> 00:21:27.090
If we do that, we might be able
to restore your memory.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:35.900
Lyria?

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:38.060
A primal beast's presence...

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.650
It's headed this way.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.170
Orchis!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.940
EPISODE 7
THE IMMORTAL PRIMAL BEAST

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.140
Next episode, "The Immortal Primal Beast."
